            <div xml:id="d866">

                <pb facs="0914" n="816" sameAs="frus:frus1920v01/pg816"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/1091</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Tenney</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-06-01"><hi rendition="#italic">June 1,
                        1920</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received June 28.]</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 3245</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to enclose a copy of the
                    text of the note sent by the Chinese Ministry of Foreign Affairs to the Japanese
                    Minister on the 22nd ultimo. I succeeded in obtaining the text of the note only
                    yesterday, hence the delay.</p>
                <p>It is reported that the Japanese response is to increase the number of Japanese
                    soldiers along the Shantung Railway.</p>
                <p>The ruling faction at Peking would undoubtedly prefer to negotiate with the
                    Japanese, but public sentiment is so strong upon the question that they are
                    afraid of a popular uprising if they consent to negotiate.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles D. Tenney</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d866-a1.xml" xpointer="d866-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
